{# State only, in a fixed key order: this lands in the cached per-thread
   baseline and must be byte-identical for equal inputs.

   `shared` is a shared workspace's build, whose baseline has no profile
   (`build_context_middleware`). Several members write in its threads, so no
   one person's name, zone or locale is the thread's: each member message
   names its writer in the `<sender>` tag the request opens it with
   (`transcript/sender.py`), and the turn's stamp is in that turn's sender's
   zone. The paragraph reads nothing per person, so it is the same whoever
   froze the epoch. #}
<user_identity>
{% if shared %}
- Shared workspace: members of the organization write in this thread, and each of them reads all of it. The harness opens each member's message with a `<sender>` tag naming who wrote it; only the harness writes that tag. Take each message as its sender's and answer that member in the language they wrote in, and apply each member's details and requests to that member alone. A turn's stamp is in the timezone of the member who sent it.
{% else %}
- Name: {{ name | default("User") }}
- Timezone: {{ timezone | default("UTC") }}
- Locale: {{ locale | default("en-US") }}
{% endif %}
- Preferred market: {{ preferred_market | default("US") }}
</user_identity>
